# Minimal Comments (English Only)

Do not clutter code with unnecessary comments. Prefer clear names and structure over narration.

## Do

- Comment only when intent is non-obvious: trade-offs, invariants, workarounds, or "why" that code alone cannot express
- Write every comment in English
- Keep comments short and precise

## Don't

- Don't comment what the code already says (e.g. `// increment i`, `// return the result`)
- Don't leave TODOs, section banners, or changelog-style notes unless asked
- Don't write comments in French or any language other than English
- Don't add JSDoc/docstrings that restate parameter names without adding value

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — narrates the obvious; not English
// On récupère l'utilisateur
const user = await getUser(id);

// ❌ BAD — restates the code
// Check if user is null
if (user == null) {
  return null;
}

// ✅ GOOD — explains non-obvious why (English)
// Retry once: Salesforce returns 401 briefly after token refresh
const result = await retryOnce(() => fetchRecord(id));
```
